+{
+  "parent_document_id": "DF-RVW-002",
+  "report_edition": "1.0/57",
+  "date": "2026-10-15",
+  "step": "4.18",
+  "phase": "REVIEW",
+  "input_zip_sha256": "d4abe62657a23695f48bfa8f0f63619ec7547ddef4f9371917ab5ad5fec3979f",
+  "source_path": "02-Documentation/DocumentIdentity/02-Structure/DF-DID-005 - Document Identity Schema.md",
+  "source_sha256": "b0097caac12209188d8e63ba9e0757cc5630945a7be5a5570b4634a7b7abd6bc",
+  "source_bytes": 7345,
+  "source_unchanged": true,
+  "received_edition": "V1.0 R0;Family Documentation;Type Structure;Component Document Identity;Author Arnaldo Figueira;Canonical/Baseline1.0;English",
+  "coverage": "Complete source13 chapters,all numbered bodies,2 structural views,3 cardinality blocks,3 cardinality/ownership rows,6 interactions,4 principle groups,3 constraint groups,4 dependencies;selected peers only",
+  "section_map": [
+    {
+      "number": "1",
+      "title": "Purpose",
+      "body": "\n\nThis document defines the canonical schema of the **Document Identity** component.\n\nThe schema specifies the logical organization of the information that constitutes a document identity while remaining independent of implementation technologies, storage mechanisms, serialization formats, and programming languages.\n\nIts purpose is to establish a stable architectural contract that can be consistently interpreted by all components of the Documentation Framework.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "c74409d93c2b01b7ff1fd158dc9fdc2934c481a427bff8e77251ee2e6265fa5b"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "2",
+      "title": "Introduction",
+      "body": "\n\nA Document Identity is represented by a well-defined collection of logical elements.\n\nThe schema specifies:\n\n- which elements compose a document identity;\n- the role of each element;\n- the cardinality of each element;\n- the constraints governing the schema.\n\nThe schema does **not** define:\n\n- physical storage;\n- XML, JSON or YAML representations;\n- database schemas;\n- programming language classes;\n- identifier generation algorithms.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "c260655bdff197be2e1302beb4926f23fca18dcaa42158854d32d5d1adbba5e2"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "3",
+      "title": "Canonical Schema",
+      "body": "\n\nThe canonical schema of a Document Identity is illustrated below.\n\n```text\n\n                    Document Identity\n                    │\n                    ├── Identity Domain\n                    │\n                    ├── Identifier\n                    │\n                    └── Identity References\n\n```\n\nEach element has a single architectural responsibility.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "126e95555bad1dd6de8efab4617bf9673d7af467f0d66a1a89f619ae82f92abb"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4",
+      "title": "Schema Elements",
+      "body": "\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.1",
+      "title": "Identity Domain",
+      "body": "\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.1.1",
+      "title": "Purpose",
+      "body": "\n\nDefines the architectural scope in which an identity is guaranteed to be unique.\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "f90896d9de9ee2827bfa64379df526fade17f73676b0569f416b753384c8b583"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.1.2",
+      "title": "Cardinality",
+      "body": "\n\n```text\n\n    Exactly one\n\n```\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "f2dbcb3bf67cdc1dacf8d4d9f434460763d5860469de4c5bb216eb5d03667d07"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.1.3",
+      "title": "Characteristics",
+      "body": "\n\n- mandatory;\n- immutable;\n- permanent.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "77416f2df62ed8eaf11ff73cba8917e164018e76ac958e8f2bed8b096b2d32f5"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.2",
+      "title": "Identifier",
+      "body": "\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.2.1",
+      "title": "Purpose",
+      "body": "\n\nRepresents the canonical identifier of the document.\n\nThe identifier is the external representation of the document identity.\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "397caced3844ed8c4ddb8c771b1fc720161c28466850f8bfbfc3708ccbcd2418"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.2.2",
+      "title": "Cardinality",
+      "body": "\n\n```text\nExactly one\n```\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "4631e1bf87b76070717988b828e9c6902640b18251d7da542a206ccbaf1ca6c1"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.2.3",
+      "title": "Characteristics",
+      "body": "\n\n- mandatory;\n- unique;\n- immutable;\n- permanent.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "c7369de321d390ca0aaf99a00a17e833e4729b05a90c130b0aa8547aada69802"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.3",
+      "title": "Identity References",
+      "body": "\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.3.1",
+      "title": "Purpose",
+      "body": "\n\nRepresents references made by other Documentation Framework components to the document identity.\n\nIdentity References are logical associations.\n\nThey are not part of the identifier itself.\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "ed7f61f2501725bba0bd4a4e428c76627a4b883ede8693a8a14c530710ad435a"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.3.2",
+      "title": "Cardinality",
+      "body": "\n\n```text\n\n    Zero or more\n\n```\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "a787a8df8abe3e2a72ab34372d41d1f0879f4174b1bb271add2696c51a7e407c"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.3.3",
+      "title": "Characteristics",
+      "body": "\n\n- optional;\n- extensible;\n- implementation independent.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "05806094325bd78c818a051d96ac41598e02f2bf3e6d665e4ff785d53145ef2e"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "5",
+      "title": "Cardinality",
+      "body": "\n\n| Element | Cardinality |\n|----------|-------------|\n| Identity Domain | 1 |\n| Identifier | 1 |\n| Identity References | 0..N |\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "01b773aac79ecf7ecb97d3625f3b0577d45a3c081ef74e1c78f8e3292ff0e63c"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "6",
+      "title": "Logical Relationships",
+      "body": "\n\n```text\n\n                                 ┌───────────────────┐\n                                 │ Document Identity │\n                                 └───────────────────┘\n                                           │\n                  ┌────────────────────────┼────────────────────────┐\n                  │                        │                        │\n                  ▼                        ▼                        ▼\n\n           Identity Domain            Identifier           Identity References\n\n```\n\nThe schema is intentionally minimal.\n\nAdditional behaviour is specified by other documents within the component.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "5a82037220e41d6f6da3cd6c253064999fea3ad611888a72f9a10fbb797e4d4f"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "7",
+      "title": "Schema Principles",
+      "body": "\n\nThe Document Identity Schema follows the following principles.\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "8a0733d9e09f3edb9d0e06aef5288a199e0b97721a7daf7a7a62d85f7c349ea5"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "7.1",
+      "title": "Single Responsibility",
+      "body": "\n\nEach schema element has one clearly defined architectural purpose.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "3d72e25b5bf3a5067e154aebf430f47bc589c23cc4a4d01eacf81880553289a6"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "7.2",
+      "title": "Stability",
+      "body": "\n\nThe schema shall remain stable throughout successive framework versions.\n\nExtensions shall preserve backward compatibility.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "2a1226cba818dfac59d94a082fbc8d9393a816935b4b849bcfbe76f7cc8cfab7"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "7.3",
+      "title": "Canonical Representation",
+      "body": "\n\nEvery document identity shall conform to the same logical schema.\n\nAlternative implementation representations shall preserve the canonical model.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "2b62621a5ac9cec22f70ae5d3d6fbfc8a38293b577156d5bb6119212b3d4509d"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "7.4",
+      "title": "Technology Independence",
+      "body": "\n\nThe schema is independent from:\n\n- programming languages;\n- databases;\n- serialization formats;\n- repositories;\n- storage mechanisms.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "e09960ac4609a83af967b544060c092c483b9627a45a8147cb5dd4b40f6936a0"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "8",
+      "title": "Schema Constraints",
+      "body": "\n\nThe following architectural constraints apply.\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "5f850c3c4e9ef02228be89cbcecc07bc3861e379efcd66c7153331d31a6e2d9c"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "8.1",
+      "title": "Identity Domain",
+      "body": "\n\n- shall exist;\n- shall never change after identity assignment.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "90746407de070e8f392dc0921d9d1427e39795b1abb3318dce31b4df8cb4a618"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "8.2",
+      "title": "Identifier",
+      "body": "\n\n- shall exist;\n- shall be unique;\n- shall remain immutable;\n- shall never be reassigned.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "fc2c4296776304a538a77f8564ac57f6edb19060baa46af0cad2d63f0ac247e7"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "8.3",
+      "title": "Identity References",
+      "body": "\n\n- shall reference existing document identities;\n- shall never redefine document identities;\n- shall remain external to the identifier.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "a98144516520cbb90c26c6ba5e3408255bc75b35e279a374b6dfbf1fc1ac1c4c"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "9",
+      "title": "Ownership",
+      "body": "\n\nThe ownership of each schema element is defined below.\n\n| Schema Element | Owner |\n|----------------|-------|\n| Identity Domain | Document Identity |\n| Identifier | Document Identity |\n| Identity References | Document Identity |\n\nOther Documentation Framework components may reference these elements but shall not redefine them.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "34465723f9ad893b562265893852a2a18a02d161c17c5433f1015d7de145fe10"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "10",
+      "title": "Relationship with Other Components",
+      "body": "\n\nThe schema defined by this component is consumed by other Documentation Framework components.\n\n| Component | Usage |\n|-----------|-------|\n| Metadata | Associates metadata with document identities. |\n| Classification | Classifies identified documents. |\n| Registry | Registers canonical document identities. |\n| Relationships | Creates semantic relationships between document identities. |\n| Knowledge Graph | Represents document identities as graph entities. |\n| Governance | Governs documents while preserving identity stability. |\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "5a2a700d7009789a9958adcc08b6d30f14607069a28451d3772e048c6bcb49cd"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "11",
+      "title": "Extensibility",
+      "body": "\n\nThe schema has been designed to support future extensions.\n\nFuture versions may introduce additional schema elements provided that:\n\n- the canonical schema remains backward compatible;\n- document identity remains stable;\n- existing identifiers remain valid;\n- architectural principles are preserved.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "d922693420b0028944663d4be0c36f77367b9940c9b8f45818a3395d6411ce93"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "12",
+      "title": "Dependencies",
+      "body": "\n\nThis document depends upon:\n\n- DF-DID-001 — Document Identity Architecture\n- DF-DID-002 — Document Identity Concepts\n- DF-DID-003 — Document Identity Model\n- DF-DID-004 — Document Identity Elements\n\nThe schema defined herein provides the foundation for lifecycle, validation, governance and specification documents that follow.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "6966c6434c13d98cfb9d7e66ca28d6846d49b4ea0c02674db4d60c9539a9188c"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "13",
+      "title": "Summary",
+      "body": "\n\nThe Document Identity Schema defines the canonical logical organization of a document identity within the Documentation Framework.\n\nIt establishes the mandatory architectural elements, their cardinalities, relationships and constraints while remaining completely independent of implementation technologies.\n\nThis schema serves as the normative architectural contract that all implementations of the Documentation Framework shall preserve.\n\n---\n\n**End of Document**\n\n---",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "b88a17e1046afd4c712b6cd929105d05af49de722d260bbedb6248195dce4d9e"
+    }
+  ],
